    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "(Scheffé 1959, Graybill 1961, Williams 1962). In these expressions, $F$ is again the ratio of observed mean squares defined by Equation 18.18, and $F_U$ and $F_L$ are the upper and lower $F$ values associated with $(\\alpha/2)$ at $(N-1)$, $(T-N)$ degrees of freedom. Specifically, $F_U = F_{(N-1),(T-N),(\\alpha/2)}$ whereas $F_L = 1/(F_{(T-N),(N-1),(\\alpha/2)})$. (See Example 2 for an application of this equation.)",
      "source_page": 577,
      "printed_page": 557,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p011:b9"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        622.0,
        1029.0,
        794.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        577
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          72.0,
